# do not delete me
#
# Git tracks files, not directories, so this directory would vanish from
# the next clone without a file in it. This is that file. It ignores
# nothing on purpose — see `keepMarker` in schemas/cat-harness.ts.
#
# docs/
# Documentation about the Knowledge Graph itself: the pages of the published
# site, some written by people and some generated from the graph. Also holds
# `reference/harness.config.example.json`, the worked example of an instance
# config that the installation guide tells a reader to copy into their
# content repository and that `package.json` `files` ships in the npm
# tarball — a reference asset, published with the site rather than rendered
# as a page. It sat at the repository root until 2026-10-06 (bean `ar1s`,
# phase 3: tooling leaves the root before the repo split).
